<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.house.keeps ~ keep ~ the host half of the keep rite

`lares rite keep workspace=<name>` runs on the host and carries the house as a bundle sealed under the house's keep key: it guards the bound workspace, flushes the shore, runs `keep-cut` in the vessel, then commits `<into>`, rebases, pushes, and lands the tessera at the bundle id the pushed tree holds. `--if-due` keeps only where the house moved since the bundle its remote-tracking branch holds (or a keep still waits for its push or landing), and with no `--workspace` reads the configured keep workspace: the one call `down` makes. `--sessions` / `--no-sessions` keeps the sensoriums or leaves them; with neither, LARES_KEEP_SESSIONS decides. A keep run by hand offers a spent lei's refill.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ keep · if-due

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`keep` params=`workspace/keep ~ keep into the bound workspace`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`if-due` params=`if-due/true ~ keep only where the house moved`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ workspace · into · accept-omissions · face · if-due · sessions

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`workspace` params=`takes/name ~ the bound workspace the bundle lays into`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`into` params=`takes/path ~ the path inside the workspace`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`accept-omissions` params=`~ land the bundle though some memory stays behind`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/index ~ the keep's face, a whole persona index from 0`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`if-due` params=`~ keep only where the house moved since the last kept bundle`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sessions` params=`~ keep the sensoriums too; --no-sessions leaves them`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand ~ host git commits and pushes; the vessel half spends a return of the keep lei strung for the workspace`>>
```

